      "content": "I cannot run a simulation on external documents or real-city conditions, as I lack the capability to process private files or perform live traffic modeling for Santiago. However, I can explain theoretically that integrating fixed-timer systems with current AI benefits usually requires a hybrid approach, such as using AI only for predictive diagnostics and emergency rerouting rather than real-time green-light signaling. This would address the \"black box\" concern by making decisions explicit while retaining some adaptive capabilities, though it often still involves a temporary trade-off in peak-hour efficiency.",
